{"task_id": "Mbpp/7", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import List\n\ndef _tokenize_whitespace(input_string: str) -> List[str]:\n    \"\"\"Splits the input string into tokens based on whitespace.\n    Punctuation attached to words remains part of the token.\n    \"\"\"\n    return input_string.split()\n\ndef find_char_long(input_string: str) -> List[str]:\n    \"\"\"Finds words that are at least 4 characters long in an input string.\n    Tokens are split by whitespace, preserving original casing and spelling.\n    \"\"\"\n    tokens = _tokenize_whitespace(input_string)\n    return [t for t in tokens if len(t) >= 4]\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/8", "solution": "To implement the software design, the following code is generated across two files: `src/square_nums.py` and `tests/test_square_nums.py`.\n\n```python\n# src/square_nums.py\n\ndef _is_numeric(value):\n    \"\"\"Checks if a value is an integer or a float.\n    This is a module-private helper function.\n    \"\"\"\n    return isinstance(value, (int, float))\n\ndef validate_input(numbers):\n    \"\"\"Validates that the input is a list and all its elements are numeric.\n    Raises TypeError if validation fails.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(numbers, list):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input 'numbers' must be a list.\")\n    for element in numbers:\n        if not _is_numeric(element):\n            raise TypeError(f\"All list elements must be numeric, but got {type(element).__name__}.\")\n\ndef square_nums(numbers):\n    \"\"\"Computes element-wise squares for a list of numbers.\n    It preserves input order and length, raising TypeError for invalid inputs.\n    \"\"\"\n    validate_input(numbers)\n    return [x * x for x in numbers]\n\n```\n\n```python\n# tests/test_square_nums.py\n\nimport unittest\nfrom src.square_nums import square_nums\n\nclass ValidationTest:\n    \"\"\"Helper class to encapsulate the example assertion for FR5.\n    It provides a run method to check the example's correctness.\n    \"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, example_input, expected_output):\n        self.example_input = example_input\n        self.expected_output = expected_output\n\n    def run(self):\n        \"\"\"Calls square_nums with example_input and compares to expected_output.\"\"\"\n        return square_nums(self.example_input) == self.expected_output\n\nclass TestSquareNums(unittest.TestCase):\n    \"\"\"Unit tests for the square_nums function, verifying FR1..FR6.\"\"\"\n\n    def test_example(self):\n        \"\"\"Verifies the example assertion (FR5) using ValidationTest.\"\"\"\n        example_input = list(range(1, 11))\n        expected_output = [x * x for x in example_input]\n        validation_test = ValidationTest(example_input, expected_output)\n        self.assertTrue(validation_test.run())\n\n    def test_empty_list(self):\n        \"\"\"Verifies the function returns an empty list for empty input (FR4).\"\"\"\n        self.assertEqual(square_nums([]), [])\n\n    def test_non_numeric_elements_raise_type_error(self):\n        \"\"\"Verifies TypeError is raised for lists containing non-numeric elements (FR6).\"\"\"\n        with self.assertRaises(TypeError):\n            square_nums([1, 2, 'a', 4])\n        with self.assertRaises(TypeError):\n            square_nums([1, None, 3])\n        with self.assertRaises(TypeError):\n            square_nums([1, [2], 3])\n\n    def test_non_list_input_raises_type_error(self):\n        \"\"\"Verifies TypeError is raised if the input is not a list (FR6 derived from BR6).\"\"\"\n        with self.assertRaises(TypeError):\n            square_nums(123)\n        with self.assertRaises(TypeError):\n            square_nums(\"not a list\")\n        with self.assertRaises(TypeError):\n            square_nums(None)\n        with self.assertRaises(TypeError):\n            square_nums((1, 2, 3)) # Tuple is not a list\n\n    def test_mixed_numeric_types(self):\n        \"\"\"Verifies correct squaring for lists containing mixed integer and float types.\"\"\"\n        self.assertEqual(square_nums([1, 2.0, 3]), [1, 4.0, 9])\n        self.assertEqual(square_nums([0.5, 2]), [0.25, 4])\n\n    def test_negative_numbers(self):\n        \"\"\"Verifies correct squaring of negative numbers.\"\"\"\n        self.assertEqual(square_nums([-1, -2, -3]), [1, 4, 9])\n        self.assertEqual(square_nums([-1.5]), [2.25])\n\n    def test_zero(self):\n        \"\"\"Verifies correct squaring when zero is an element.\"\"\"\n        self.assertEqual(square_nums([0]), [0])\n        self.assertEqual(square_nums([0, 1, -1]), [0, 1, 1])\n\n```"}
