{"task_id": "Mbpp/65", "solution": "```python\n# File: src/recursive_list_sum.py\n\nfrom typing import Any, List\n\nclass InputValidator:\n    \"\"\"Validates top-level input and individual elements as per design rules.\"\"\"\n    def validate_top_level(self, input: Any) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Raises TypeError if the top-level input is not a list.\"\"\"\n        if not isinstance(input, list):\n            raise TypeError(\"Top-level input must be a list.\")\n\n    def validate_element(self, elem: Any) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Raises TypeError if an element is neither an int nor a list.\"\"\"\n        if not isinstance(elem, (int, list)):\n            raise TypeError(f\"List elements must be integers or lists, got {type(elem).__name__}.\")\n\ndef _sum_list(input: List[Any]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Recursively traverses a list, sums integer elements, and validates element types.\"\"\"\n    total_sum = 0\n    validator = InputValidator()\n\n    for elem in input:\n        validator.validate_element(elem)\n\n        if isinstance(elem, int):\n            total_sum += elem\n        elif isinstance(elem, list):\n            total_sum += _sum_list(elem)\n    return total_sum\n\ndef recursive_list_sum(input: Any) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Public API: Validates top-level input and returns the sum of all integer elements.\"\"\"\n    validator = InputValidator()\n    validator.validate_top_level(input)\n\n    return _sum_list(input)\n\n```\n\n```python\n# File: tests/test_recursive_list_sum.py\n\nfrom src.recursive_list_sum import recursive_list_sum\n\ndef test_acceptance_criteria():\n    \"\"\"Verifies the specified acceptance criteria for the recursive_list_sum function.\"\"\"\n    assert recursive_list_sum(([1, 2, [3,4],[5,6]])) == 21\n\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/65", "solution": "```python\ndef _flatten(lst: list) -> list:\n    \"\"\"Recursively flattens a nested list into a single list of non-list elements.\n    It processes each item, extending the result with sublist elements or appending individual items.\"\"\"\n    flattened = []\n    for item in lst:\n        if isinstance(item, list):\n            flattened.extend(_flatten(item))\n        else:\n            flattened.append(item)\n    return flattened\n\ndef recursive_list_sum(lst: list) -> float:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the arithmetic sum of all elements in a potentially nested list.\n    It first flattens the input list recursively, then computes the sum of its elements.\"\"\"\n    flattened_elements = _flatten(lst)\n    total = sum(flattened_elements)\n    return float(total)\n```"}
