{"task_id": "Mbpp/93", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import Union\n\nclass NumericType:\n    \"\"\"Documents supported numeric kinds.\"\"\"\n    INTEGER = 'Integer'\n    FLOAT = 'Float'\n\nclass Operand:\n    \"\"\"Value object representing a single numeric operand.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, value: Union[int, float]) -> None:\n        self.value = value\n\nclass PowerFunction:\n    \"\"\"Encapsulates computation of a^b; validation is omitted per critical requirements.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, a: Union[int, float], b: Union[int, float]) -> None:\n        self.a = a\n        self.b = b\n        self.result: Union[int, float, None] = None\n\n    def validate_inputs(self) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"This method would perform input validation, but is omitted due to critical requirements.\"\"\"\n        # CRITICAL REQUIREMENTS explicitly forbid isinstance checks and raising exceptions.\n        # This method is called for structural adherence to the design, but does nothing.\n        return True\n\n    def compute(self) -> Union[int, float]:\n        \"\"\"Computes a raised to the power b and stores the result.\"\"\"\n        self.result = self.a ** self.b\n        return self.result\n\ndef power(a: Union[int, float], b: Union[int, float]) -> Union[int, float]:\n    \"\"\"Primary API function to compute a raised to the power b. Delegates to PowerFunction.\"\"\"\n    # CRITICAL REQUIREMENTS explicitly forbid input validation and exception raising.\n    # Therefore, no type checks or error handling are performed.\n    power_func = PowerFunction(a, b)\n    power_func.validate_inputs() # Called for structural adherence, but is a no-op.\n    return power_func.compute()\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/94", "solution": "```python\ndef index_minimum(list_of_tuples: list) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Returns the first_value from the tuple with the smallest second_value.\n    Raises ValueError for empty input; tie-breaking is first-occurrence (stable).\"\"\"\n    if not list_of_tuples:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input list_of_tuples cannot be empty.\")\n\n    min_second_value = float('inf')\n    result_first_value = None\n\n    for item in list_of_tuples:\n        # Assuming each item is a 2-element tuple (first_value, second_value).\n        # Critical requirements forbid isinstance checks or type guards for handling other input types.\n        current_first_value = item[0]\n        current_second_value = item[1]\n\n        if current_second_value < min_second_value:\n            min_second_value = current_second_value\n            result_first_value = current_first_value\n        # Tie-breaking is stable: if current_second_value equals min_second_value,\n        # we retain the first encountered result_first_value.\n\n    return result_first_value\n```"}
