{"task_id": "Mbpp/95", "solution": "```python\n\"\"\"Implementation of Find_Min_Length(list_of_lists) per SRS.\nExposes the public API Find_Min_Length and its helpers.\n\"\"\"\nfrom typing import List, Any\n\ndef validate_input(list_of_lists: Any) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Validate outer list and inner elements per SRS.\n    Raises TypeError or ValueError as specified for invalid input.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(list_of_lists, list):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input must be a list of lists.\")\n    if not list_of_lists:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input list of lists cannot be empty.\")\n    for inner_list in list_of_lists:\n        if not isinstance(inner_list, list):\n            raise TypeError(\"All elements within the outer list must be lists.\")\n\ndef compute_lengths(list_of_lists: List[List]) -> List[int]:\n    \"\"\"Return the lengths of each inner list.\n    This list of integers is used to determine the minimum length.\n    \"\"\"\n    return [len(inner_list) for inner_list in list_of_lists]\n\ndef Find_Min_Length(list_of_lists: List[List]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Public API - returns int minimum inner-list length, or raises TypeError/ValueError per SRS.\n    Orchestrates validation, computation, and result determination.\n    \"\"\"\n    validate_input(list_of_lists)\n    lengths = compute_lengths(list_of_lists)\n    return min(lengths)\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/96", "solution": "```python\ndef divisor(n):\n    \"\"\"Counts the number of positive divisors for a given integer n.\n    Assumes n is a positive integer.\n    \"\"\"\n    count = 0\n    i = 1\n    while i * i <= n:\n        if n % i == 0:\n            if i * i == n:\n                count += 1\n            else:\n                count += 2\n        i += 1\n    return count\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/96", "solution": "```python\ndef divisor(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Counts the number of positive divisors for a given integer.\n    Includes 1 and the number itself. Handles zero and negative inputs.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n\n    m = abs(n)\n    count = 0\n    i = 1\n    while i * i <= m:\n        if m % i == 0:\n            if i * i == m:\n                count += 1\n            else:\n                count += 2\n        i += 1\n    return count\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/97", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import Any, Dict, List\n\ndef frequency_lists(lists: List[List[Any]]) -> Dict[Any, int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Flattens a list of lists and counts the occurrences of each element.\n    Returns a dictionary mapping each distinct element to its frequency.\n    \"\"\"\n    frequencies: Dict[Any, int] = {}\n    for nested_list in lists:\n        for element in nested_list:\n            frequencies[element] = frequencies.get(element, 0) + 1\n    return frequencies\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/98", "solution": "def multiply_num(sequence):\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes the product of all elements in a sequence and divides by its length.\n    Raises ZeroDivisionError if the input sequence is empty.\n    \"\"\"\n    length = len(sequence)\n\n    if length == 0:\n        raise ZeroDivisionError(\"Input sequence cannot be empty.\")\n\n    product = 1\n    for num in sequence:\n        product *= num\n\n    result = product / length\n    return float(result)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/97", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import Iterable, Any, Dict\n\ndef frequency_lists(list_of_lists: Iterable[Iterable[Any]]) -> Dict[Any, int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Flatten the provided iterable of iterables and return a dict mapping each element to its integer frequency.\n    Elements are assumed to be hashable.\n    \"\"\"\n    frequency_dict: Dict[Any, int] = {}\n\n    for sublist in list_of_lists:\n        for element in sublist:\n            # Increment the count for the current element.\n            frequency_dict[element] = frequency_dict.get(element, 0) + 1\n            \n    return frequency_dict\n```"}
