{"task_id": "Mbpp/106", "solution": "```python\n# src/add_lists.py\nfrom typing import List, Tuple, Any\n\n__all__ = ['add_lists']\n\ndef add_lists(input_list: List[Any], input_tuple: Tuple[Any, ...]) -> Tuple[Any, ...]:\n    \"\"\"Return a new tuple containing elements of input_tuple followed by elements of input_list without mutating inputs.\n    The order of elements from both inputs is preserved.\n    \"\"\"\n    result = input_tuple + tuple(input_list)\n    return result\n```\n```python\n# tests/test_add_lists.py\nfrom src.add_lists import add_lists\n\ndef test_add_lists_example():\n    \"\"\"Verify the example assertion from the design specification.\"\"\"\n    assert add_lists([5, 6, 7], (9, 10)) == (9, 10, 5, 6, 7)\n\ndef test_add_lists_non_mutation():\n    \"\"\"Verify that the input list and tuple are not mutated by the function.\"\"\"\n    original_list = [1, 2, 3]\n    original_tuple = (4, 5)\n    \n    # Take snapshots of inputs before calling the function\n    list_snapshot = list(original_list)\n    tuple_snapshot = tuple(original_tuple)\n    \n    # Call the function\n    result = add_lists(original_list, original_tuple)\n    \n    # Assert that the original inputs remain unchanged\n    assert original_list == list_snapshot\n    assert original_tuple == tuple_snapshot\n    \n    # Optionally, verify the result itself\n    assert result == (4, 5, 1, 2, 3)\n\ndef test_add_lists_empty_inputs():\n    \"\"\"Verify behavior with empty input lists and tuples.\"\"\"\n    # Test with empty list\n    assert add_lists([], (1, 2)) == (1, 2)\n    # Test with empty tuple\n    assert add_lists([1, 2], ()) == (1, 2)\n    # Test with both empty\n    assert add_lists([], ()) == ()\n    # Test with mixed types and empty inputs\n    assert add_lists([None, \"test\"], ()) == (None, \"test\")\n    assert add_lists([], (\"hello\", None)) == (\"hello\", None)\n```"}
