{"task_id": "Mbpp/138", "solution": "def _generate_powers_of_two_up_to(n: int):\n    \"\"\"\n    Yields non-zero powers of two (2^k, k>=1) in descending order, up to n.\n    For n < 2, no powers are yielded.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n < 2:\n        return\n\n    # Find the largest power of two (2^k, k>=1) that is less than or equal to n.\n    current_power = 1\n    while current_power * 2 <= n:\n        current_power *= 2\n\n    # Yield powers in descending order until 2 (which is 2^1).\n    while current_power >= 2:\n        yield current_power\n        current_power //= 2\n\n\ndef _can_represent(n: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Determines if n can be represented as a sum of one or more non-zero powers of two (2^k, k>=1),\n    allowing repeated powers. Uses a greedy approach with generated powers.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n % 2 != 0:\n        return False  # All non-zero powers of two are even, so their sum must be even.\n\n    # A greedy approach effectively finds if n can be formed.\n    remaining_n = n\n    for power in _generate_powers_of_two_up_to(n):\n        while remaining_n >= power:\n            remaining_n -= power\n        if remaining_n == 0:\n            break\n\n    return remaining_n == 0\n\n\ndef is_Sum_Of_Powers_Of_Two(n: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if an integer n can be represented as a sum of one or more non-zero powers of two (2^k, k>=1).\n    Returns False for any integer n < 2.\n    \"\"\"\n    # CRITICAL REQUIREMENT: \"Do NOT add isinstance() checks... Trust the caller's inputs\".\n    # Therefore, explicit type validation (e.g., raising TypeError) is omitted despite design specification.\n\n    # Handle edge cases and base conditions for n < 2.\n    if n < 2:\n        return False\n\n    # Orchestrate the representation check using internal helpers.\n    return _can_represent(n)"}
