{"task_id": "Mbpp/222", "solution": "```python\ndef check_type(t: tuple) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if all elements in the tuple share the same runtime type.\n    Returns True for empty or single-element tuples.\n    \"\"\"\n    if len(t) == 0:\n        return True\n\n    first_type = type(t[0])\n    for e in t[1:]:\n        if type(e) is not first_type:\n            return False\n\n    return True\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/222", "solution": "```python\n# tuple_type_checker/__init__.py\nfrom tuple_type_checker.tuple_checker import TupleChecker\n\ndef check_type(t) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Public API per FR1. Delegates to TupleChecker.check_type and returns bool or propagates TypeError.\"\"\"\n    return TupleChecker().check_type(t)\n\n# tuple_type_checker/tuple_checker.py\nfrom tuple_type_checker.type_validator import TypeValidator\nfrom tuple_type_checker.result import Result\n\nclass TupleChecker:\n    \"\"\"Implements TupleChecker domain service that drives validation, element-type collection, and uniformity decision.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, type_validator: TypeValidator = None):\n        # Default injection of TypeValidator if none provided for testability.\n        self._type_validator = type_validator or TypeValidator()\n\n    def check_type(self, t: tuple) -> bool:\n        # Raises TypeError if not tuple per FR3 through TypeValidator.validate_input.\n        self._type_validator.validate_input(t)\n        types_set = self._type_validator.get_element_types(t)\n        # An empty set or single-type set indicates uniformity (BR7 recommended behavior).\n        is_uniform = (len(types_set) <= 1)\n        return is_uniform\n\n# tuple_type_checker/type_validator.py\nclass TypeValidator:\n    \"\"\"Encapsulates input validation and element-type extraction logic.\"\"\"\n    def validate_input(self, t) -> bool:\n        if not isinstance(t, tuple):\n            raise TypeError(\"Input must be a tuple\")\n        return True\n\n    def get_element_types(self, t: tuple) -> set:\n        # Returns a set of type objects from the tuple elements.\n        return {type(e) for e in t}\n\n# tuple_type_checker/result.py\nclass Result:\n    \"\"\"Simple container for the boolean result of the homogeneity check.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, is_uniform: bool):\n        self.is_uniform = is_uniform\n```"}
