{"task_id": "Mbpp/223", "solution": "def _lower_bound(arr, start, end, x):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the first index i in [start, end) where arr[i] >= x.\n    Returns end if no such element is found.\n    \"\"\"\n    low = start\n    high = end\n    while low < high:\n        mid = low + (high - low) // 2\n        if arr[mid] < x:\n            low = mid + 1\n        else:\n            high = mid\n    return low\n\ndef _upper_bound(arr, start, end, x):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the first index i in [start, end) where arr[i] > x.\n    Returns end if no such element is found.\n    \"\"\"\n    low = start\n    high = end\n    while low < high:\n        mid = low + (high - low) // 2\n        if arr[mid] <= x:\n            low = mid + 1\n        else:\n            high = mid\n    return low\n\ndef is_majority(arr, n, x):\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if element x is the majority in the first n elements of a sorted array.\n    A majority element occurs more than considered_n / 2 times.\n    \"\"\"\n    considered_n = min(n, len(arr))\n\n    if considered_n == 0:\n        return False\n\n    first_occurrence_idx = _lower_bound(arr, 0, considered_n, x)\n    \n    # If x is not present in the considered portion, it cannot be a majority.\n    if first_occurrence_idx == considered_n or arr[first_occurrence_idx] != x:\n        return False\n\n    last_occurrence_idx_plus_one = _upper_bound(arr, 0, considered_n, x)\n    \n    occurrences = last_occurrence_idx_plus_one - first_occurrence_idx\n    \n    return occurrences > considered_n / 2"}
