{"task_id": "Mbpp/252", "solution": "```python\nimport math\n\ndef convert(number):\n    \"\"\"Converts a numeric input to polar coordinates (r, theta).\n    This function processes int, float, or complex numbers directly.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Convert input to complex to uniformly extract real and imaginary parts.\n    complex_number = complex(number)\n    real_part = complex_number.real\n    imag_part = complex_number.imag\n\n    # Compute magnitude (r) using the built-in abs function.\n    r = abs(number)\n    # Compute angle (theta) using math.atan2 for correct quadrant handling.\n    theta = math.atan2(imag_part, real_part)\n\n    # Return the polar coordinates as a tuple of two floats.\n    return (float(r), float(theta))\n```"}
