{"task_id": "Mbpp/252", "solution": "```python\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\nimport math\n\n@dataclass\nclass ComplexNumber:\n    \"\"\"Represents a complex number with real and imaginary parts.\"\"\"\n    real: float\n    imag: float\n\n@dataclass\nclass PolarCoordinate:\n    \"\"\"Represents polar coordinates with magnitude and phase.\"\"\"\n    r: float\n    theta: float\n\ndef sqrt(x: float) -> float:\n    \"\"\"Wrapper for math.sqrt.\"\"\"\n    return math.sqrt(x)\n\ndef atan2(y: float, x: float) -> float:\n    \"\"\"Wrapper for math.atan2.\"\"\"\n    return math.atan2(y, x)\n\ndef _compute_magnitude(c: ComplexNumber) -> float:\n    \"\"\"Computes the magnitude (r) of a complex number.\"\"\"\n    return sqrt(c.real**2 + c.imag**2)\n\ndef _compute_phase(c: ComplexNumber) -> float:\n    \"\"\"Computes the phase (theta) of a complex number.\"\"\"\n    return atan2(c.imag, c.real)\n\ndef convert(value) -> tuple[float, float]:\n    \"\"\"Converts a complex or real number to polar coordinates (r, theta).\"\"\"\n    if isinstance(value, complex):\n        c_num = ComplexNumber(real=value.real, imag=value.imag)\n    else: # Handles int or float inputs.\n        c_num = ComplexNumber(real=float(value), imag=0.0)\n\n    r = _compute_magnitude(c_num)\n    theta = _compute_phase(c_num)\n\n    return (float(r), float(theta))\n```"}
