{"task_id": "Mbpp/273", "solution": "```python\n# src/substract_elements.py\n\ndef validate_arguments(a: tuple, b: tuple) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Validates inputs for type and length.\n    Raises TypeError if not tuples, ValueError if lengths differ.\"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(a, tuple) or not isinstance(b, tuple):\n        raise TypeError(\"Both inputs must be tuples.\")\n    if len(a) != len(b):\n        raise ValueError(\"Input tuples must have equal length.\")\n\ndef compute(a: tuple, b: tuple) -> tuple:\n    \"\"\"Performs element-wise subtraction and returns a new tuple.\n    Assumes inputs are valid tuples of equal length.\"\"\"\n    return tuple(a[i] - b[i] for i in range(len(a)))\n\ndef substract_elements(a: tuple, b: tuple) -> tuple:\n    \"\"\"Subtracts elements of the second tuple from the first, element-wise.\n    Inputs must be tuples of equal length, otherwise raises appropriate errors.\"\"\"\n    validate_arguments(a, b)\n    return compute(a, b)\n\n```\n```python\n# src/__init__.py\n\nfrom .substract_elements import substract_elements\n\n```\n```python\n# tests/test_substract_elements.py\n\nimport pytest\nfrom src.substract_elements import substract_elements\n\ndef test_substract_elements_example():\n    \"\"\"Verifies the core functionality with the provided example assertion.\"\"\"\n    assert substract_elements((10, 4, 5), (2, 5, 18)) == (8, -1, -13)\n\ndef test_substract_elements_type_error():\n    \"\"\"Ensures TypeError is raised for non-tuple inputs.\"\"\"\n    with pytest.raises(TypeError, match=\"Both inputs must be tuples.\"):\n        substract_elements([1, 2], (3, 4))\n    with pytest.raises(TypeError, match=\"Both inputs must be tuples.\"):\n        substract_elements((1, 2), [3, 4])\n    with pytest.raises(TypeError, match=\"Both inputs must be tuples.\"):\n        substract_elements(1, 2)\n\ndef test_substract_elements_length_mismatch():\n    \"\"\"Confirms ValueError is raised when tuple lengths differ.\"\"\"\n    with pytest.raises(ValueError, match=\"Input tuples must have equal length.\"):\n        substract_elements((1, 2, 3), (4, 5))\n    with pytest.raises(ValueError, match=\"Input tuples must have equal length.\"):\n        substract_elements((1, 2), (3, 4, 5))\n\ndef test_substract_elements_empty_tuples():\n    \"\"\"Tests correct behavior with empty tuples.\"\"\"\n    assert substract_elements((), ()) == ()\n\ndef test_substract_elements_single_element_tuples():\n    \"\"\"Checks operation with single-element tuples.\"\"\"\n    assert substract_elements((5,), (2,)) == (3,)\n\ndef test_substract_elements_float_elements():\n    \"\"\"Verifies support for float elements.\"\"\"\n    assert substract_elements((10.5, 4.0), (2.1, 5.0)) == pytest.approx((8.4, -1.0))\n\n```"}
