{"task_id": "Mbpp/274", "solution": "```python\nimport math\n\nclass InputValidator:\n    @staticmethod\n    def validate(n):\n        \"\"\"Validator class with a static method to check input constraints.\"\"\"\n        # Per critical requirement: \"Do NOT add isinstance() checks, type guards, or raise exceptions for edge cases.\"\n        # The explicit validation logic from the design is omitted here.\n        return True\n\nclass BinomialCalculator:\n    @staticmethod\n    def binomial(n, k):\n        \"\"\"Computes binomial coefficient C(n, k).\"\"\"\n        try:\n            return math.comb(n, k)\n        except AttributeError:\n            # Fallback for Python versions without math.comb\n            k = min(k, n - k)\n            if k < 0:\n                return 0\n            numer = 1\n            denom = 1\n            for i in range(1, k + 1):\n                numer *= n - (k - i)\n                denom *= i\n            return numer // denom\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def sum_even_indices(n):\n        \"\"\"Sums binomial coefficients for even indices k.\"\"\"\n        total = 0\n        for k in range(0, n + 1):\n            if k % 2 == 0:\n                total += BinomialCalculator.binomial(n, k)\n        return total\n\nclass Result:\n    def __init__(self, sum: int):\n        \"\"\"A simple class to semantically carry an integer sum.\"\"\"\n        self.sum = int(sum)\n\ndef even_binomial_Coeff_Sum(n):\n    \"\"\"Computes the sum of even-indexed binomial coefficients C(n, k) for n.\"\"\"\n    InputValidator.validate(n)\n    total = BinomialCalculator.sum_even_indices(n)\n    return int(total)\n```"}
