{"task_id": "Mbpp/277", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import Dict, Any, TypeVar\n\n# Define type variables for keys and values for internal class generality\nK = TypeVar('K')\nV = TypeVar('V')\n\nclass Entry:\n    \"\"\"Simple holder for a key/value pair representing a domain entry.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, key: K, value: V) -> None:\n        self.key = key\n        self.value = value\n\nclass Dictionary:\n    \"\"\"Thin wrapper around a native dict; stores entries and exposes get_items() for the underlying mapping.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, entries: Dict[K, V]) -> None:\n        self._entries = entries\n\n    def get_items(self) -> Dict[K, V]:\n        \"\"\"Returns the underlying dict mapping.\"\"\"\n        return self._entries\n\nclass DictFilter:\n    \"\"\"Encapsulates the filtering algorithm, producing a Dictionary instance with entries where value >= n.\"\"\"\n    def dict_filter(self, dictionary: Dict[K, V], n: V) -> Dictionary:\n        \"\"\"Iterates input mapping, selects key/value pairs where value >= n, and returns a Dictionary instance.\"\"\"\n        filtered_entries: Dict[K, V] = {}\n        for key, value in dictionary.items():\n            if value >= n:\n                filtered_entries[key] = value\n        return Dictionary(filtered_entries)\n\ndef dict_filter(dictionary: Dict[str, int], n: int) -> Dict[str, int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Public entry point to filter a dictionary to entries with values >= n.\n    Delegates filtering to DictFilter and returns a native dict result.\n    \"\"\"\n    filter_service = DictFilter()\n    filtered_dictionary_obj = filter_service.dict_filter(dictionary, n)\n    return filtered_dictionary_obj.get_items()\n\n__all__ = ['dict_filter']\n```"}
