{"task_id": "Mbpp/409", "solution": "def min_product_tuple(input_list):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the minimum product of two-element numeric tuples in a list.\n    Assumes input_list is non-empty and contains valid 2-element numeric tuples.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Initialize the minimum product with the product of the first tuple.\n    # This relies on the critical requirement to \"Trust the caller's inputs\",\n    # implying the input list will be non-empty and well-formed.\n    first_element = input_list[0]\n    current_min_product = first_element[0] * first_element[1]\n\n    # Iterate through the rest of the tuples to find the smallest product.\n    # This is a single-pass O(n) algorithm using O(1) extra space.\n    for i in range(1, len(input_list)):\n        a, b = input_list[i]\n        product = a * b\n        if product < current_min_product:\n            current_min_product = product\n\n    return current_min_product"}
