{"task_id": "Mbpp/433", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import Sequence, List\n\nclass Number:\n    \"\"\"Represents a numeric value from the domain model.\"\"\"\n    value: float\n\n    def __init__(self, value: float):\n        self.value = float(value)\n\nclass Element:\n    \"\"\"Represents an item in an Array with a numeric value.\"\"\"\n    value: Number\n\n    def __init__(self, value: float):\n        self.value = Number(value)\n\nclass Array:\n    \"\"\"Represents a collection of Element objects.\"\"\"\n    elements: List[Element]\n\n    def __init__(self, elements_sequence: Sequence[float]):\n        self.elements = [Element(e) for e in elements_sequence]\n\nclass Result:\n    \"\"\"Holds the boolean result of the comparison.\"\"\"\n    value: bool\n\n    def __init__(self, value: bool):\n        self.value = value\n\ndef check_greater(array: Sequence[float], number: float) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if 'number' is strictly greater than every element in 'array'.\n    It returns True if so, otherwise False.\n    \"\"\"\n    target_number = Number(number)\n    domain_array = Array(array)\n\n    is_greater_than_all = True\n    for element_obj in domain_array.elements:\n        if not (target_number.value > element_obj.value.value):\n            is_greater_than_all = False\n            break\n\n    final_result = Result(is_greater_than_all)\n    return final_result.value\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/432", "solution": "```python\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\n\n@dataclass\nclass Trapezium:\n    \"\"\"Holds the three numeric sides provided by the caller: baseA, baseB, and sideC.\"\"\"\n    baseA: float\n    baseB: float\n    sideC: float\n\n@dataclass\nclass Result:\n    \"\"\"A container for the numeric median value.\"\"\"\n    value: float\n\nclass MedianCalculator:\n    \"\"\"Encapsulates the median computation logic.\"\"\"\n    def computeMedian(self, t: Trapezium) -> float:\n        \"\"\"Returns the median of a trapezium, computed as (baseA + baseB) / 2.\"\"\"\n        return (t.baseA + t.baseB) / 2.0\n\n@dataclass\nclass FunctionCall:\n    \"\"\"Models an invocation, mapping caller inputs to domain objects for traceability.\"\"\"\n    a: float\n    b: float\n    c: float\n\n    def invoke(self) -> float:\n        \"\"\"Constructs domain objects, performs the median calculation, and returns the result.\"\"\"\n        trapezium_instance = Trapezium(baseA=self.a, baseB=self.b, sideC=self.c)\n        calculator = MedianCalculator()\n        median_value = calculator.computeMedian(trapezium_instance)\n        # Result dataclass is used internally for semantic mapping.\n        _result_object = Result(value=median_value)\n        return median_value\n\ndef median_trapezium(a: float, b: float, c: float) -> float:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the median length of a trapezium using only arguments 'a' and 'b'.\n    Argument 'c' is accepted for the signature but ignored in the computation.\n    \"\"\"\n    call = FunctionCall(a=a, b=b, c=c)\n    return call.invoke()\n```"}
