{"task_id": "Mbpp/459", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import List\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\n\n@dataclass\nclass InputString:\n    \"\"\"A domain helper for wrapping input strings.\"\"\"\n    value: str\n\n@dataclass\nclass OutputString:\n    \"\"\"A domain helper for wrapping output strings.\"\"\"\n    value: str\n\nclass Character:\n    \"\"\"Encapsulates a single character and its properties.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, value: str) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Initializes Character with a single-character string.\"\"\"\n        self.value = value\n\n    def isUppercase(self) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Checks if the character is an ASCII uppercase letter.\"\"\"\n        return 'A' <= self.value <= 'Z'\n\ndef remove_uppercase(input: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Removes ASCII uppercase characters from the input string while preserving order.\"\"\"\n    input_obj = InputString(input)\n    retained_chars: List[str] = []\n\n    for ch in input_obj.value:\n        character_obj = Character(ch)\n        if not character_obj.isUppercase():\n            retained_chars.append(ch)\n            \n    result_str = \"\".join(retained_chars)\n    output_obj = OutputString(result_str)\n    return output_obj.value\n```"}
