{"task_id": "Mbpp/563", "solution": "```python\nimport re\n\ndef _find_quoted_substrings(s: str) -> list[str]:\n    \"\"\"Return raw substrings between matching double quotes found in s, in occurrence order.\n    This helper uses a non-greedy regular expression to capture content within quotes.\n    \"\"\"\n    return re.findall(r'\"(.*?)\"', s)\n\ndef extract_values(s: str) -> list[str]:\n    \"\"\"Public API: Accepts a single argument of type string and returns a list of extracted strings.\n    It locates quoted substrings, strips leading/trailing whitespace, and preserves their original order.\n    \"\"\"\n    raw_values = _find_quoted_substrings(s)\n    trimmed_values = [value.strip() for value in raw_values]\n    return trimmed_values\n```"}
