{"task_id": "Mbpp/602", "solution": "```python\n# first_repeated_char.py\n\ndef first_repeated_char(input: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Finds the first repeated character in a string.\n    Returns the character whose second occurrence appears earliest. Returns \"\" if no repeat is found.\"\"\"\n    seen_chars = set()\n    for char in input:\n        if char in seen_chars:\n            return char\n        seen_chars.add(char)\n    return \"\"\n\n```\n```python\n# test_example.py\n\nfrom first_repeated_char import first_repeated_char\n\n# Required exact assertion (must appear verbatim):\nassert first_repeated_char(\"abcabc\") == \"a\"\n\ndef run_test_example() -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Runs the specified test assertion.\n    Returns True if the assertion passes, otherwise an AssertionError is raised.\"\"\"\n    from first_repeated_char import first_repeated_char\n    assert first_repeated_char(\"abcabc\") == \"a\"\n    return True\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    # This block allows running the test example as a script.\n    print(\"Running test_example.py...\")\n    if run_test_example():\n        print(\"All assertions in test_example.py passed successfully!\")\n\n```"}
