{"task_id": "Mbpp/731", "solution": "```python\n# src/lateralsurface_cone.py\nimport math\n\nPI: float = math.pi\n\"\"\"Module-level constant for mathematical PI.\"\"\"\n\ndef computeSlantHeight(r: float, h: float) -> float:\n    \"\"\"Computes the slant height of a right circular cone.\"\"\"\n    return math.sqrt(r*r + h*h)\n\ndef computeLateralArea(r: float, l: float) -> float:\n    \"\"\"Computes the lateral surface area given radius and slant height.\"\"\"\n    return PI * r * l\n\ndef lateralsurface_cone(r: float, h: float) -> float:\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes the lateral surface area of a right circular cone.\n    This is the public entry point for the module.\n    \"\"\"\n    l = computeSlantHeight(r, h)\n    lateral_area = computeLateralArea(r, l)\n    return lateral_area\n```\n\n```python\n# tests/test_lateralsurface_cone.py\nfrom src.lateralsurface_cone import lateralsurface_cone\n\ndef test_sample_assertion():\n    \"\"\"\n    Verifies the lateral surface area calculation against a known sample.\n    Uses the provided sample assertion value.\n    \"\"\"\n    assert lateralsurface_cone(5, 12) == 204.20352248333654\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/731", "solution": "```python\nimport math\n\ndef lateralsurface_cone(r, h):\n    # Computes the lateral surface area of a right circular cone.\n    # r is the radius, h is the height.\n    s = math.sqrt(r * r + h * h)\n    lateral = math.pi * r * s\n    return float(lateral)\n```"}
