{"task_id": "Mbpp/743", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import List, Any\n\ndef _effective_rotation_count(count: int, length: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the effective right rotation count.\n    Uses modulo operator, handling zero length to prevent errors.\"\"\"\n    if length == 0:\n        return 0\n    return count % length\n\ndef _rotate_copy(items: List[Any], shift: int) -> List[Any]:\n    \"\"\"Returns a new list with elements rotated right by 'shift' positions.\n    A shift of 0 returns a shallow copy of the original list.\"\"\"\n    if shift == 0:\n        return list(items)\n    return items[-shift:] + items[:-shift]\n\ndef rotate_right(items: List[Any], count: int) -> List[Any]:\n    \"\"\"Rotates a list of items to the right by the specified count, returning a new list.\n    Handles empty lists and computes an effective rotation count based on list length.\"\"\"\n    length = len(items)\n    if length == 0:\n        return []\n\n    effective_shift = _effective_rotation_count(count, length)\n    return _rotate_copy(items, effective_shift)\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/743", "solution": "def rotate_right(lst, k):\n    \"\"\"\n    Rotates the elements of a list to the right by k positions.\n    Returns a new list with elements rotated as specified.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(lst)\n    if n == 0:\n        return []\n\n    k_mod = k % n\n    if k_mod == 0:\n        return list(lst)  # Return a new list if no effective rotation\n\n    return list(lst[-k_mod:]) + list(lst[:-k_mod])"}
