{"task_id": "Mbpp/759", "solution": "```python\nimport re\n\ndef is_decimal(input_string) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if a string is a decimal number with exactly two digits after the point.\n    It performs a full regex match against the pattern ^\\\\d+\\\\.\\\\d{2}$.\"\"\"\n    \n    # The design recommends the regex: ^\\d+\\.\\d{2}$\n    decimal_pattern = r\"^\\d+\\.\\d{2}$\"\n    \n    # Use re.fullmatch to ensure the entire string matches the pattern\n    match = re.fullmatch(decimal_pattern, input_string)\n    \n    # Convert the match object (or None) to a boolean\n    return bool(match)\n```"}
