{"task_id": "Mbpp/763", "solution": "```python\ndef find_min_diff(seq, n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes the minimum absolute difference between any two distinct elements\n    among the first n elements of seq.\n    Validation is omitted as per CRITICAL REQUIREMENTS.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Extract the first n elements and sort them to facilitate finding min difference.\n    sub_seq = sorted(seq[:n])\n\n    min_diff = float('inf')\n\n    # Iterate through adjacent elements in the sorted sub-sequence.\n    # The minimum absolute difference between any two elements must exist between adjacent ones in a sorted list.\n    for i in range(n - 1):\n        diff = sub_seq[i+1] - sub_seq[i]\n        if diff < min_diff:\n            min_diff = diff\n            \n    return min_diff\n```"}
