{"task_id": "Mbpp/775", "solution": "```python\ndef odd_position(lst: list) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if every element at an odd index is an odd integer.\n    Vacuously true for lists with less than two elements.\"\"\"\n\n    # Handle vacuous truth for lists of length 0 or 1.\n    if len(lst) < 2:\n        return True\n\n    # Iterate over odd indices: 1, 3, 5, ... up to len(lst) - 1.\n    for i in range(1, len(lst), 2):\n        value = lst[i]\n\n        # Check if the value is an odd integer.\n        # Type checking for 'int' is forbidden; non-numeric values may cause TypeError.\n        if not (abs(value) % 2 == 1):\n            return False\n\n    # If the loop completes, all values at odd indices were odd integers.\n    return True\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/775", "solution": "def odd_position(input_list: list) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if every element at an odd index (1, 3, 5, ...) in the list is an odd integer.\n    Returns True if all such elements are odd, or if there are no odd indices.\n    \"\"\"\n    for i in range(1, len(input_list), 2):\n        # Retrieve the value at the current odd index.\n        value = input_list[i]\n        # Check if the value is even. If so, the condition is not met.\n        if value % 2 == 0:\n            return False\n    # If the loop completes, all elements at odd indices were odd, or there were no odd indices.\n    return True"}
