{"task_id": "Mbpp/786", "solution": "from dataclasses import dataclass\n\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\nclass IndexResult:\n    \"\"\"Minimal typed wrapper representing the returned integer index.\n    This dataclass is for conceptual mapping as per design.\n    \"\"\"\n    index: int\n\ndef right_insertion(sequence: list, value) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes the right (after-last-equal) insertion index for a value in a sorted sequence.\n    Precondition: sequence is sorted in non-decreasing order; elements are comparable to value.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(sequence)\n    low = 0\n    high = n\n\n    while low < high:\n        mid = low + (high - low) // 2\n        if sequence[mid] <= value:\n            low = mid + 1\n        else:\n            high = mid\n    \n    return low"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/786", "solution": "def right_insertion(lst: list, value: any) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Locates the right insertion point for a value in a sorted ascending list.\n    The index returned is immediately after the last equal element.\n    \"\"\"\n    low = 0\n    high = len(lst)\n\n    # Implements right-biased binary search.\n    # It finds the first index i such that lst[i] > value.\n    while low < high:\n        mid = (low + high) // 2\n        if lst[mid] <= value:\n            low = mid + 1\n        else:\n            high = mid\n    return low"}
